    <section id="using-invoiz"><h2>1. Using INVOIZ</h2><p>INVOIZ connects buyers, sellers and delivery partners through an online marketplace. These terms apply when you create an account, submit an application or use marketplace and logistics services. Read them together with our <a href="{{ route('legal.privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a> and the order details shown before you confirm a purchase.</p><p>You must be legally able to make the transaction or have the authorization required by applicable law. Do not use someone else's identity or payment account without permission.</p></section>
    <section id="accounts"><h2>2. Your account</h2><p>Provide accurate account, contact and delivery information, and keep it up to date. Keep your password and verification codes private. You are responsible for activity you authorize through your account; contact support promptly if you suspect unauthorized access.</p><p>Seller and logistics access may require an application, supporting documents and approval. Account access can be restricted where verification is incomplete, an account is compromised or there is evidence of misuse. An account restriction does not remove valid refund, payment or privacy obligations.</p></section>
    <section id="orders"><h2>3. Orders and prices</h2><p>Review the product, variant, quantity, delivery address, payment method, shipping fees, voucher discount and final total before placing an order. A checkout containing several stores can create separate orders with separate delivery fees and payment requirements.</p><p>Placing an order submits it for processing; stock, payment verification and seller acceptance still apply. Product information and availability are supplied by the relevant seller. If an order cannot be fulfilled, use the order and support channels to arrange cancellation or another appropriate remedy.</p></section>
    <section id="payments"><h2>4. Payments and settlement</h2><p>Use only payment methods and receiving details displayed in INVOIZ for your order.</p><ul><li><strong>Cash on delivery:</strong> pay the amount due to the authorized delivery partner when your order is delivered.</li><li><strong>GCash:</strong> check the store's receiving QR, account name and exact amount in your own GCash app before sending payment. Upload a separate, genuine receipt for each store when requested. INVOIZ does not need your GCash PIN or OTP.</li></ul><p>Uploading a receipt does not automatically confirm payment. The seller checks the actual incoming payment. For GCash orders, the seller must forward the full order payment, including shipping, to the platform's designated receiving account. Admin must confirm the full deposit before the seller can accept the order. The platform's escrow and remittance records track this settlement process; an uploaded image alone does not transfer funds.</p><p>Stakeholder shares are settled through the platform's payout process after the applicable delivery and settlement requirements are met. Riders must not collect a second cash payment for a prepaid GCash order. Raise any payment mismatch or request to pay an unexpected account through support before sending more money.</p></section>
    <section id="delivery"><h2>5. Delivery</h2><p>Provide an accurate address, recipient name and reachable phone number. Sellers and delivery partners use these details to arrange pickup and delivery. Delivery timing can be affected by service coverage, availability, weather, access restrictions or an unsuccessful delivery attempt.</p><p>Use the order's tracking information for updates. Do not share a delivery verification code before receiving the parcel, and report missing, damaged or incorrect items promptly.</p></section>
    <section id="returns"><h2>6. Cancellations, returns and refunds</h2><p>Use the cancellation or return option on the relevant order when available. Available actions depend on the order's progress and the return settings applicable to that purchase. Provide an accurate explanation and relevant evidence, and retain the item and packaging while a claim is being reviewed.</p><p>A request is subject to review; submitting it does not by itself confirm a refund. If a control is unavailable or you need help, contact the seller or INVOIZ Support. Nothing in these terms removes rights to an appropriate remedy for defective, unsafe, misdescribed or undelivered goods under applicable consumer law. An in-app return window does not override rights that the law provides.</p></section>
    <section id="seller-responsibilities"><h2>7. Seller and delivery-partner responsibilities</h2><p>Sellers must have the right to sell their products, keep listings and stock accurate, disclose relevant product information and charges, and fulfill accepted orders responsibly. Sellers must not list unlawful, counterfeit or prohibited goods, submit false payment evidence or deduct their share before forwarding a required full GCash deposit.</p><p>Delivery and logistics partners must follow the assigned delivery and remittance process and safeguard parcels and customer information. All participants must use customer details only for legitimate order, delivery, support and legal purposes, rather than unrelated marketing or harassment.</p></section>
    <section id="acceptable-use"><h2>8. Acceptable use and content</h2><p>Do not commit fraud, abuse vouchers, impersonate others, manipulate reviews, upload harmful files, interfere with the service or attempt to access another person's private records. Listings, messages, reviews and uploaded documents must be lawful and must respect other people's rights.</p><p>Only submit content you are entitled to provide. By submitting content for a listing, review, application or support request, you allow INVOIZ to display or process it as needed for that service. Avoid including unrelated personal or financial information in screenshots and messages.</p></section>
    <section id="account-closure"><h2>9. Account closure and service changes</h2><p>Buyers can request account deletion from their account settings. The current process provides a 30-day grace period to cancel the request. Unresolved orders, deliveries, refunds, disputes or settlements may place the request on hold.</p><p>{{ config('account_deletion.retention_notice') }}</p><p>Service availability can be affected by maintenance or technical issues. Policy updates will be posted on these pages with an updated date. Updates must respect applicable law and existing consumer and privacy rights.</p></section>
    <section id="support"><h2>10. Support, disputes and your rights</h2><p>Start with the order's seller or the <a href="{{ url('/help#report') }}">Help Center</a> for purchase concerns. For account, payment or policy questions, email <a href="mailto:{{ config('support.email') }}">{{ config('support.email') }}</a>. Do not include passwords, GCash PINs or OTPs in a support request.</p><p>These terms are subject to applicable Philippine law and do not exclude rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded. You can also refer consumer concerns to the appropriate government authority. See the Department of Trade and Industry's <a href="https://fairtrade.dti.gov.ph/faq/is-no-return-no-exchange-policy-allowed/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">guidance on returns and consumer remedies</a>.</p></section>
